## Hints for Future Agents
- updateFrontMatter appends a missing key at the end of the block, so a plan without Parent gets it after StatusNote, unlike create, which writes it after Type. There is no positional insert.
- canonicalReference already prefixes "parent: " on a plan lookup failure, so runSetParent returns its error unwrapped. A wrapped "Parent: %w" trips staticcheck ST1005 (capitalised error string), as an earlier commit found.
- parentCycle walks parentChain from the new parent upward and reports the chain if the plan itself appears; a pre-existing cycle among the new parent's ancestors that does not involve the plan is not refused, planner check already reports it.
- The post-commit hook pushes master. `git -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null commit` keeps a commit local.

## Codebase Discoveries
completer.parents is shared by create --parent, set status --superseded-by, and now set parent; passing args through is harmless for create (its args are name words) and useful for the other two.

